    "title": "Erdogan's Upcoming Visits to Ethiopia and Somalia",
    "text": "• Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan will visit Ethiopia and Somalia in the first two months of 2025.\n• The announcement was made by Erdogan and reported by Al Mayadeen News on March 8, 2024.\n• Erdogan previously visited Gulf Arab states, including Saudi Arabia and Qatar, in July 2023 to seek funds and strengthen ties.\n• The upcoming visits aim to reinforce regional ties and support political and economic cooperation in the Horn of Africa.\n• Erdogan's visits follow his efforts to broker a peace deal between Ethiopia and Somalia.\n• The key goals of the visits include strengthening bilateral relations, solidifying the peace deal, and enhancing trade and cultural exchanges.\n• Erdogan's previous visits to Gulf Arab states focused on economic cooperation and financial support.\n• The visits are significant for Turkey's growing influence in the Horn of Africa and may lead to greater economic engagement and regional integration.\n• Erdogan's diplomatic moves reflect Turkey's strategy to diversify international alliances and create alternative economic blocs.",
